<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="44168" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/ENGL/482/44168.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2025" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025.xml">2025</calendarYear><term id="120251" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring.xml">Spring 2025</term><subject id="ENGL" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/ENGL.xml">English</subject><course id="482" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/ENGL/482.xml">Writing Technologies</course></parents><sectionNumber>1G </sectionNumber><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>SP25 - ENGL 482 - Writing Technologies - John Gallagher - This class examines the impact writing technologies have on our reading and writing practices. The class will investigate the relationship between today’s digital platforms, i.e., Twitter, Reddit, Snapchat, as well as earlier methods of writerly communication such as cuneiform tablets, paper, and the printing press. We will address some of the challenges writing technologies pose, including the role of social media and artificial intelligence.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>CrossListOpen (Restricted)</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2025-01-21Z</startDate><endDate>2025-05-07Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>02:00 PM</start><end>02:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>MWF    </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>44</roomNumber><buildingName>English Building</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Gallagher" firstName="J">Gallagher, J</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>